@ldz1216 @jlongster , I fixed the issue with PR #33471.

When the user switched models in the UI, local.model.set() only updated the local persisted store. The server's SessionTable.model was only updated when a prompt arrived with a different model: field. The session runner resolved models using SessionTable.model, causing image/vision capability checks to fail with the wrong model between the UI switch and the next message.

The fix adds a POST /api/session/{sessionID}/model endpoint that publishes ModelSwitched immediately, keeping server state in sync with the UI.

